    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0418" n="1152" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1152"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your note of the 20th ultimo, in which you state that Her Majesty’s
                    Government agrees to pay one-third of the expense of the surveys of the Samoan
                    land commission, aggregating, perhaps, $2,000, provided the Government of the
                    United States concurs.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to inform you that this Government will assume one-third of that
                    expense, and that the German ambassador here has been so advised in reply to his
                    note upon the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
